//! The `reading-flow` [CSS](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS) property enables
//! modifying the `reading order` of child elements of a
//! [block](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Glossary/Block/CSS),
//! [flex](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/Guides/Flexible_box_layout), or
//! [grid](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/Guides/Grid_layout) layout. This affects
//! the order in which they are rendered to speech and navigated to when using sequential navigation
//! such as tabbing to links or buttons.
//!
//! Initial: normal. Inherited: no.
//! Percentages: not accepted.
//!
//! Grammar: normal | source-order | flex-visual | flex-flow | grid-rows | grid-columns | grid-order
//!
//! Specification: https://drafts.csswg.org/css-display-4/#propdef-reading-flow
//!
//! Author guide: https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/Reference/Properties/reading-flow
//!
//! Purpose and value descriptions adapted from MDN contributors (CC-BY-SA-2.5).
//!
//! Generated from @webref/css 8.7.8. Do not edit.

